    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-278311",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275712/assets/58be29819a83484e2a524e33c27dc2d890dfc722c28d787afded5bc811f898d8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
